This repository contains an independent, educational re-implementation written for
learning purposes. It is NOT the PICT solver and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
its authors.

The reference implementation it studies is:

    PICT - A Differentiable, GPU-Accelerated Multi-Block PISO Solver for
    Simulation-Coupled Learning Tasks in Fluid Dynamics
    https://github.com/tum-pbs/PICT
    Journal of Computational Physics, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2025.114433
    arXiv: https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16992
    Copyright the PICT authors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

No PICT source code is redistributed here. Where this port mirrors a PICT design
decision, the corresponding C++/CUDA function and line number is cited in comments and
in docs, so the reader can look it up in the upstream repository.

This work is likewise licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).
